      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Feline asthma is characterized by the presence of inflammation and bronchoconstriction. The diagnosis is based on history-taking, clinical and radiographic signs, bronchoalveolar lavage, and response to therapy. Treatment focuses primarily on eliminating the inflammation and reversing bronchoconstriction. This article contains an analysis of new therapeutic avenues, including inhalers."},
